package.lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml

# ── Generated output. None of it is hand-edited, so formatting it is at best
# wasted work and at worst a rewrite of an artifact something else owns.
#
# `dist/` is what ships to npm (the package publishes only `dist/`), so a
# `--write` pass run after `pnpm build` rewrites the published artifact rather
# than the source it came from.
dist/
# Typedoc output, and it is *committed* (87 tracked files) — reformatting it
# produces a real diff that looks like an authored change.
docs/
# nyc / coverage reporters. Gitignored, which makes a rewrite invisible to git
# rather than harmless.
coverage/
.nyc_output/
.kilo_cov/

# ── `example/` is a git submodule: its own repository
# (github.com/fivexer/assignment-matcher-site), its own toolchain, and no
# prettier config of its own. Formatting it from here applied *this* repo's
# style to 54 source files in a repo this one does not own — plus walking its
# 14MB Vite build and its gitignored vendored mermaid bundle, which together
# made `pnpm prettier` take over two minutes.
#
# If the demo site should be prettier-formatted, that is a decision to make
# inside that repo with its own config, not a side effect of formatting this one.
example/
